<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · mountain</p><h1 class="enc-title">Monte Titano</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Monte Titano is a limestone mountain in San Marino, rising to 739 metres, on whose ridge stand the City of San Marino and the republic's Three Towers. According to tradition <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saint-marinus">Saint Marinus</a> founded a Christian community there in 301. The mountain and the historic centre of the city were inscribed as a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/unesco-world-heritage-site">UNESCO World Heritage Site</a> in 2008.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/monte-titano.jpg" alt="Monte Titano" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Francesco Bini · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:San_marino,_veduta_del_monte_titano_02.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
